## Establish the staged ontology Generate contract and baseline evaluation

Context: Task 1 of the `staged-ontology-generate` plan. Generate is being
refactored from a one-shot LLM call into a durable three-stage wizard
(detect → human review → checkpointed relations/attributes/axioms
completion) that appends to the existing ontology instead of replacing it.
This entry establishes the approved design, the `agent_owl_generator` SPEC
target contract, and the expanded eval dataset ahead of any runtime code
change, per the AI Feature Lifecycle gate (`.cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc`).
No runtime source code was changed.

Changes:

1. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-20-three-stage-ontology-generate-design.md
   New design doc capturing the approved three-stage Generate architecture:
   Stage 1 detection inputs/outputs, Stage 2 human review (add/remove/
   include/exclude/edit + alternate labels, at-least-one-entity invariant,
   locked existing anchors), the durable versioned draft and source
   fingerprint/invalidation contract, stable entity identity across rename,
   Stage 3 strict relations→attributes→axioms ordering with per-substage
   checkpoints and resume, the append-only final merge, the no-reparse
   contract, and removal of the post-generation pitfall rewrite loop in
   favor of prompt-first constraints and reject-only validation.
2. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md
   Fully updated for the staged material change: four staged entry points
   (`detect_entities`, `infer_relations`, `infer_attributes`,
   `infer_axioms`) marked `(staged, planned)` alongside the still-current
   one-shot `run_agent` contract; a new §3a structured-schema section for
   candidate entities and locked anchors; three new staged success-criteria
   examples; eight new proposed staged eval dimensions (§5) with a proposed
   ≥0.95 aggregate, explicitly not yet in `tests/eval/thresholds.yaml`; a
   new §6a documenting prompt-first pitfall handling, entity closure, the
   append-only merge, and the no-reparse rule; five new staged failure
   modes (§6); updated tracing requirements (draft id/revision/stage trace
   tags); and a sign-off section recording the real dry-run baseline result
   and the exact live-baseline blocker (missing Databricks credentials) —
   no run URI was fabricated.
3. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl and
   tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl
   Synced both mirrors to be byte-identical (the planning mirror was
   missing 3 legacy seed rows already present in the baseline mirror), then
   appended 12 new `staged`-tagged material-change examples covering
   detection, default inclusion, manual add/edit/remove, alternate labels,
   excluded-entity rejection, locked-anchor append/dedup, strict
   relations→attributes→axioms ordering, checkpoint recovery, stale-source
   invalidation, and no document reparse. The dataset now has 25 examples
   (10 parsed-corpus + 3 legacy + 12 staged), all unique ids, all valid
   JSONL. The 10 pre-existing parsed-corpus rows are unchanged.
4. tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py
   Added `_validate_staged_examples()` — a schema-level structural check
   (unique ids, required `input.stage`, non-empty `expected.constraints`
   with `kind`/`value`) run before the existing parsed-corpus contract
