## Fix Task 4 review findings: lifecycle gate, idempotent merge, type-hint/subClassOf validation, SKOS altLabel, payload validation

Context: Follow-up review pass on the Task 4 staged-Generate wiring (see
the entry above). Two "Important" and five "Minor" findings, fixed with
TDD (RED before each production change), no frontend files touched.

Changes:

1. src/shared/fastapi/main.py (Important #1 — lifecycle/edit locking)
   `_is_status_gated_edit` previously exempted every `/wizard/` path from
   the version-status/single-editor-lock gate, including
   `POST /ontology/wizard/generate/complete` — which actually runs the
   deterministic append-only merge and calls `domain.save()`, a genuine
   design mutation. Added `_STATUS_GATE_WIZARD_EDIT_SUFFIXES` (currently
   just `.../generate/complete`), checked *before* the blanket `/wizard/`
   exemption, so `complete` is now gated exactly like every other
   `/ontology/` write while Stage 1 `detect` and Stage 2
   `draft/update`/`draft/discard` (session-scoped draft only, never the
   persisted design) remain exempt.
2. tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py
   Added `test_generate_complete_is_gated`,
   `test_generate_review_routes_remain_exempt`,
   `test_generate_complete_get_not_gated` to `TestIsStatusGatedEdit`, and a
   new `TestGenerateCompleteLifecycleGate` class covering: `complete`
   blocked on `PUBLISHED`/`IN-REVIEW`; `complete` passes on `DRAFT` with no
   lock holder; `complete` blocked by a different lock holder on `DRAFT`;
   admins not exempt from the lock; viewer role still blocked; and the
   three review-only routes staying reachable on a locked version and
   despite another user holding the edit lock.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateDraft.py (Important #2 — durable
   merge checkpoint)
   Added a `merge_checkpoint` field (`{"status": ..., "result": ...}`,
   default `pending`), deliberately independent of `stage`/
   `completion_checkpoints`: the merge is a workflow-level step whose
   completion must be checkable across a crash between its own
   `domain.save()` and `stage` flipping to `done`, which the existing
   per-substage checkpoints cannot express. Added
   `with_merge_checkpoint()` (rejects reopening an already-`done`
   checkpoint, mirroring `with_checkpoint()`'s strictness) and wired
   serialization (`to_dict`/`from_dict`/`new`) plus self-healing
   normalization for missing/invalid persisted values.
4. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateWorkflow.py (Important #2 — idempotent
   merge; Minor #3 — type_hint validation; Minor #5 — subClassOf handling;
   Minor #7 — payload validation defense-in-depth)
   - `run_completion()`: checks `draft.merge_checkpoint` before ever
     calling `merge_draft_into_ontology()` again. If already `done`,
     short-circuits with the cached merge stats (and still finishes the
     `stage -> DONE` transition if that didn't land last time). Otherwise
     sets the checkpoint to `running`, runs the merge, sets it to `failed`
     (re-raising) or `done` accordingly. The staleness check
     (`ensure_not_stale`) is now only performed on the initial
     `REVIEWING -> COMPLETING` transition — once completion has started,
     the merge itself grows the live ontology, so re-fingerprinting the
     current source on every resume would misread that self-inflicted
     growth as drift and permanently block a legitimate resume.
   - `merge_draft_into_ontology()` is now idempotent by construction as
     defense in depth on top of the checkpoint: new classes are tagged
     `generated_from=<candidate id>` so a second call for the same draft
     recognizes and reuses already-merged classes instead of re-adding
     them under a suffixed name; object-property relations are deduped by
     `(domain, range, label)`; `disjointWith`/`equivalentClass` axioms are
     deduped by `(type, subject, sorted(objects))`; `alternate_labels` are
     deduped order-preservingly when building a new class.
   - Added an upfront reject-only check: an *included* candidate with a
     `type_hint` other than `class` raises `DraftValidationError` before
     any mutation — the ontology model only supports merging class
     candidates today, so a property-hinted candidate is rejected
     explicitly rather than silently merged as a wrongly-shaped class.
   - `subClassOf` axiom handling: an exact-repeat parent is now a silent
     no-op (idempotent); a *different* parent on a class that already has
     one raises `DraftValidationError` (the model supports only one
     `parent` per class — multi-inheritance is explicitly rejected, never
     silently dropped as before).
   - `update_draft()`: wrapped the op-dispatch body in
     `try/except (TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError)`, re-raising as
     `DraftValidationError`, so a malformed nested field (e.g. non-list
     `evidence`) that slips past the route-level shape checks still
     surfaces as a 400, never a 500.
5. tests/units/ontology/test_generate_draft.py
   Added `TestMergeCheckpoint`: defaults to `pending`; `running`/`done`/
   `failed` transitions and result storage; rejects reopening a `done`
   checkpoint; rejects an invalid status; round-trips through
   serialization; self-heals a missing or invalid persisted checkpoint to
   `pending`. Imported `CHECKPOINT_PENDING`.
6. tests/units/ontology/test_generate_workflow.py
   Added `TestSubClassOfAndDisjointAxiomMerge` (exact-repeat `subClassOf`
   deduped not errored; conflicting `subClassOf` rejected explicitly;
   `disjointWith` deduped on exact repeat), `TestTypeHintValidationInMerge`
   (`class` merges normally; `object_property`/`data_property` rejected;
   an excluded non-class candidate is never checked), and
   `TestIdempotentMerge` (checkpoint defaults `pending` before completion
   and is `done` after; a simulated crash after the merge already touched
   the live ontology but before the checkpoint write resumes idempotently
   without duplicating entities; a `done` checkpoint with `stage` still
   `completing` short-circuits and finishes the stage transition; a
   repeated `complete` call on an already-`DONE` draft is rejected).
   Removed a dead conditional in `_seed_ready_for_merge` left over from an
   earlier draft of the test helpers.
7. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py (Minor #4 — alternate_labels
   as first-class OWL data)
   `_add_class` now emits a `skos:altLabel` triple for every entry in a
   class's `alternate_labels`, using rdflib's standard `SKOS` namespace
   (consistent with the existing `RDF`/`RDFS`/`OWL` prefix usage) — the
   synonym data was previously only an in-app session field, never
   round-tripped through the OWL export/import contract.
8. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py
   `get_classes()` now reads back `skos:altLabel` triples per class into
   the parsed `alternate_labels` list (deduped, sorted for determinism).
9. tests/units/ontology/test_owl_generator.py /
   tests/units/ontology/test_owl_parser.py
   Added round-trip tests: `alternate_labels` export as `skos:altLabel`
   and re-import identically; no `alternate_labels` omits the triple
   entirely; a class with no `altLabel` parses to an empty list.
10. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py (Minor #7 — payload validation at
    the route boundary)
    `update_generate_draft` now validates payload *shapes* before calling
    into `GenerateWorkflow.update_draft`: `revision` must coerce to `int`
    (was previously an unguarded `int(revision)` that raised a raw
    `ValueError`, mapped to a 500 by `map_route_errors`); `entity`/
    `updates` must be JSON objects if present; `entity_id` must be a
    string if present. Each failure now raises `ValidationError` (400).
11. tests/units/api/test_generate_routes.py
    Added `test_update_draft_non_numeric_revision_is_400`,
    `test_update_draft_non_dict_entity_is_400`,
    `test_update_draft_non_dict_updates_is_400`,
    `test_update_draft_non_string_entity_id_is_400` to `TestDraftRoutes`.
12. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md
    Updated the "Replace instead of append" pitfall bullet and added new
    bullets documenting: the durable `merge_checkpoint` + idempotent-merge
    defense in depth against duplicate merges on crash/retry; that
    included non-`class` `type_hint` candidates are rejected, not silently
    merged; that `alternate_labels` round-trips through OWL as
    `skos:altLabel`; and that a conflicting `subClassOf` (different
    existing parent) is rejected explicitly, never silently dropped. Also
    documented that `POST /wizard/generate/complete` is lifecycle-gated
    while Stage 1/2 remain exempt.
13. changelogs/v0.9.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-09-21.log (Minor #6 — changelog
    inaccuracy)
    Corrected earlier in this file (entry 9 of the Task 4 section above):
    `require_domain_llm` runs synchronously in the `async def` route body
    before `create_task`, not "only inside the background-thread target"
    as originally stated.

