## Resumable three-step Generate wizard UI (task 5 of staged ontology generate)

Context: Task 5 (final task) of the `staged-ontology-generate` plan on
reviewed base `9eab9437` (Task 4 review fixes). Rebuilds the Ontology ->
Generate section's existing single-page wizard into a resumable three-step
in-page wizard — Configure & Detect -> Review Entities -> Complete — wired
to the five staged routes landed in Task 4, replacing every remaining
client reference to the now-410 legacy `/wizard/generate-async` one-shot
path. The attached implementation plan
(`/Users/benoit.cayla/.cursor/plans/staged-ontology-generate_6fc7e158.plan.md`)
was not edited. Followed strict TDD: `tests/units/front/
test_ontology_generate_wizard_staged.py` (39 structural/behavior contract
tests, following this repo's existing regex-on-raw-source convention for
frontend tests since there is no JS test runner) was written first and run
to an observed RED (10 failing — missing routes/functions/session keys/
stepper wiring) before any markup/JS/CSS change, then implemented to GREEN.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_wizard.html
   Restructured from one form into three stage panes under a new
   accessible stepper nav (`wizard-stepper`, `aria-label`, one `<li
   aria-current="step">` per active step): `wizardConfigurePane` (visible
   by default, wraps the existing Data Sources/Documents/Guidelines/
   Options tabs unchanged — `wizardMetadataTableBody`/`wizardDocsList`/
   `wizardGuidelines`/`wizardIncludeDataProps`/`wizardTemplateButtons` all
   preserved verbatim), `wizardReviewPane` (`ob-hidden` by default —
   stale-source banner with a "Re-detect" action, an `aria-live="polite"`
   validation banner, a read-only "Existing Entities" (locked anchors)
   card, a "Candidate Entities" card with an add-candidate form and a
   Discard Draft / disabled-by-default Continue-to-Complete footer), and
   `wizardCompletePane` (`ob-hidden` by default — a `relations -> attributes
   -> axioms -> merge` checklist with `data-substage` markers in that exact
   order, a summary block, and a Retry button). The top-right CTA keeps its
   existing id/`data-requires-llm` (`wizardTopGenerateBtn`) but is now
   relabeled "Detect Entities" and drives Stage 1 detection instead of the
   old one-shot generate. No inline `style=`/`<script>` anywhere in the
   template; tabs keep the shared `ob-tabs` treatment.
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard-review.js (new)
   Owns Stage 2 rendering/mutation only. `render(draftView)` re-renders the
   stale banner, locked-anchor rows (`renderLockedAnchorRow` — read-only,
   deliberately never wires include/exclude/remove/edit controls, per the
   design's "existing anchors cannot be edited from this screen" rule),
   candidate rows (checkbox include/exclude, editable canonical label/
   description/type-hint/evidence, a repeatable alternate-label chip
   input), and the Continue button's disabled state (stale OR zero
   entities). Every mutation (`add`/`remove`/`update`/`include`/`exclude`)
   goes through one `postDraftUpdate({op, ...})` helper that attaches the
   current `draft_revision` and POSTs to `.../draft/update`; a `409`
   response reloads the draft from the server instead of clobbering it
   (`showNotification` + `GET .../draft`), never silently retrying the
   stale write. Discard uses the shared `showConfirmDialog` (no native
   `confirm()`/`alert()`/`prompt()` anywhere in this module or
   `ontology-wizard.js`). Event handling is delegated on the pane root
   (3 `addEventListener` calls total for click/change/keydown — not one
   listener per rendered row) via `data-action` attributes
   (`wizard-review-continue`/`-discard`/`-remove-candidate`/etc.).
   Cross-module calls into `ontology-wizard.js` (Continue -> Stage 3,
   Discard success -> back to Configure, stale re-detect) go through a
   small `window.WizardCore` bridge object rather than duplicating task-
   polling/stage-transition logic here.
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js (rewritten)
   - Removed every legacy one-shot symbol (`generateOntologyFromWizard`,
     `applyWizardOntology(Silent)`, `showWizardResults`,
     `wizardGeneratedOWL`, the pitfall-refinement-round panel helpers tied
     to the old agent) and its three sessionStorage keys (`WIZARD_TASK_KEY`,
     `WIZARD_OWL_KEY`, `WIZARD_STATS_KEY`) — no code path calls
     `/wizard/generate-async` (410) anymore.
   - Added `WIZARD_DETECT_TASK_KEY`/`WIZARD_COMPLETE_TASK_KEY` — the *only*
     two sessionStorage keys this module ever writes, and only ever an
     opaque task id string (`sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, taskId)`, never
     `JSON.stringify` of a draft/entity/checkpoint). All draft/entity/
     checkpoint state is fetched fresh from `GET .../draft` on every
     resume (page load with no running task, task completion, task
     failure/cancel, server-restart/404-on-poll) — `resumeDraftFromServer()`
     is the single choke point that decides which stage to show
     (`reviewing` -> Review pane; `completing`/`done` -> Complete pane;
     no draft -> Configure pane).
   - `setWizardStage()` drives the stepper: toggles each `.wizard-step`'s
     `active`/`completed` class and sets/clears `aria-current="step"" per
     the accessible-stepper requirement.
   - `startGenerateDetection()` confirms (shared `showConfirmDialog`, not
     `window.confirm`) before discarding an in-progress Review/Complete
     draft, then POSTs `.../generate/detect` with the same metadata/
     guidelines/options/documents payload as before (unchanged ready-
     document filtering: `file.parse_status !== 'ready'`) plus the
     selected table names, stores the task id, and polls via the existing
     `/tasks/{id}` + `TaskProgressUI` overlay.
   - `startGenerateCompletion()`/`retryGenerateCompletion()` POST
     `.../generate/complete` and poll the same way; `renderCompleteChecklist
     (draft)` reads `draft.completion_checkpoints`/`draft.merge_checkpoint`
     to paint the relations/attributes/axioms/merge checklist and shows the
     Retry button only when a checkpoint is `failed` — retrying just
     re-issues the same completion call, which the server already resumes
     at the first non-`done` substage (never resets a `done` one).
     `renderCompleteChecklistFromTaskSteps()` mirrors the same checklist
     live from the polling task's `steps` while a completion is running.
   - `handleCompletionSuccess()` mirrors today's post-generate behavior:
     refresh ontology status, reload the session ontology, `SidebarNav
     .switchTo('map')`, and a `showNotification` summary of what was
     merged.
   - `window.WizardCore` exposes exactly the three calls Stage 2 needs
     (`startCompletion`, `redetect`, `onDraftDiscarded`) — no other
     surface is shared between the two files, and no task-polling logic is
     duplicated in `ontology-wizard-review.js`.
   - Stage 1 config loading (`loadWizardMetadata`/`loadWizardDocuments`/
     `loadWizardTemplatesFromServer`), table/document selection, and the
     `data-action` delegation for the Configure pane's own controls are
     unchanged from before this task.
4. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-wizard.css
   Replaced the old hard-coded-hex `.wizard-step` progress-step styling
   with design tokens (`var(--db-primary)`, `var(--db-primary-light)`,
