## Close final-review gaps for the staged ontology Generate change

Context: Closes every actionable gap from the final review of the
`staged-ontology-generate` plan (base `0fc3532d`, all five tasks + fixes
landed). The one "Important" gap — the eval harness's `--live` mode never
actually exercised the staged entry points and still imported the
deprecated one-shot `agent_owl_generator.engine.run_agent` bridge — is
fixed, a real live eval was run against the `DEFAULT` Databricks profile
and `databricks-claude-sonnet-5`, Sphinx docs were extended for the new
modules, and three minor closures (task-tracker deep link, README, typed
410 error) were applied. The attached implementation plan was not edited.
Followed TDD for every executable change: each fix has a new focused test
observed to exercise the change (RED before the fix where a prior behavior
existed to contrast against; new capability tests written test-first).

Changes:

1. tests/eval/staged_contract.py (Important — live staged eval truthfulness)
   Added a live-endpoint mode that retargets the *existing* detect-tagged
   constraint checks (`_c_all_included`, `_c_excludes_anchor`,
   `_c_excludes_anchor_alt`, `_c_min_new_candidates`, `_c_synonyms_as_alt`,
   `_c_no_separate_synonym`, `_c_does_not_parse`) from the scripted mock to
   the real Databricks Foundation Model endpoint, with zero duplicated
   scoring logic: `live_endpoint(host, token, endpoint)` (context manager)
   + `_run_detection_live()` (real `staged.detect_entities()` call, tool
   surface wired to each row's own `input.corpus`, `call_serving_endpoint`
   only *spied* — `wraps=`, not scripted) + a per-example-id cache so a row
   with N constraints costs one live call, not N. Added
   `_run_live_completion_chain()` — runs `infer_relations` ->
   `infer_attributes` -> `infer_axioms` end to end against the real
   endpoint for one representative (non-adversarial) closed entity set,
   chaining each real structured output into the next substage's
   checkpoint exactly like `GenerateWorkflow.run_completion` does in
   production, and scoring entity closure (`success`) and no-document-tool
   access (the real `tools=` kwarg observed via the same spy technique) —
   the completion-tagged dataset rows are all deliberately adversarial/
   scripted-invalid (testing rejection of a bad LLM answer), which a real
   endpoint cannot be made to reproduce on demand, so this chain is the
   representative live substitute. `score_staged_examples_live()` runs both
   and returns per-dimension + aggregate scores as **evidence for the
   record, not a second CI gate** — the enforced
   `owl_generator.staged_contract: 0.95` gate stays the deterministic/
   scripted `score_staged_examples()`, unweakened and unchanged.
2. tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py (Important)
   `_live_runner` (parsed-corpus contract, `--live`) rewritten to call the
   real `staged.detect_entities()` instead of the deprecated
   `agents.agent_owl_generator.engine.run_agent` — `detect_entities` is now
   the *only* production entry point that reads source material at all
   (SPEC §3), so it is what the parsed-corpus document-reading contract
   (`ready_corpus_use`/`no_parse_safety`/`status_disclosure`/
   `sidecar_hiding`) actually needs verified live. The observed trace is
   built the same way as before (tool-call names + every tool-result
   payload, which always echoes back the requested filename) plus the
   detected candidates' own labels/descriptions/evidence standing in for
   the free-text "reply" the removed one-shot bridge produced. `main()`
   now also calls `staged_contract.score_staged_examples_live()` under
   `--live`, logging its metrics (`staged_live_*`) into the *same* MLflow
   run as the parsed-corpus contract via a new `extra_mlflow_logging`
   callback (see #3) rather than a disconnected second run. This closes
   the **last** eval dependency on the legacy engine — `engine.py` itself
   is intentionally **not deleted**: `tests/units/agents/
   test_agent_owl_generator_truncation.py`,
   `test_agent_owl_generator_class_cap.py`, and `tests/units/pge_eval/
   test_owl_evaluator_stage.py` still exercise it directly as real
   consumers, so deletion is not safe per this change's own "only if no
   consumers remain" criterion.
3. tests/eval/document_corpus_contract.py
   `run_contract()` gained an optional `extra_mlflow_logging: Callable[[],
   None] | None` parameter, invoked once inside the existing
