## Fix root cause of the below-gate live staged score (fixture shape + missing tracing)

Context: The prior live eval (run `218202e1c9a64a6a98d4add618310e48`) scored
`staged_live_aggregate=0.850`, below the requested `0.950` bar, on
`excludes_existing_anchor_as_new`/`excludes_existing_alternate_label_as_new`.
A read-only systematic investigation established this was **not** a dedup
defect: `staged-locked-anchor-dedup-001`'s dataset metadata used
`{catalog, schema, table}` keys, but every production metadata consumer
(`agents.tools.metadata.tool_get_metadata`/`tool_get_table_detail`,
`staged.py`/`engine.py`) keys off `name`/`full_name`. Against the real
endpoint this made `get_metadata` return a table entry with `name: null`,
`get_table_detail` could not resolve it, and — since this row has no
`input.corpus` fallback to ground the model any other way — the model
replied with prose instead of JSON, so `detect_entities` rejected the
malformed answer *before its anchor-dedup logic ever ran*. The reported
anchor/alt-label failures were downstream of that rejection, not independent
dedup misses. `staged-detect-new-entities-001` had the identical malformed
shape but happened to PASS live because its `input.corpus` grounded the
model independently of the broken metadata tool — masking the bug. The same
investigation found `--live` never called `agents.tracing.setup_tracing()`,
so the `@trace_agent`/`@trace_llm`/`@trace_tool` decorators already on the
staged entry points silently no-opped and the live run carried zero
trace/span evidence. Followed TDD: each fix below has a test written and
observed RED against the pre-fix code before the fix landed.

Changes:

1. tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl +
   .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl (dataset fixture
   fix, mirrors kept byte-identical)
   Corrected the 4 staged rows whose `input.metadata.tables` entries used
   the stale `{catalog, schema, table}` shape
   (`staged-detect-new-entities-001`, `staged-default-inclusion-001`,
   `staged-locked-anchor-dedup-001`, `staged-no-one-shot-default-001`) to
   the real production shape (`name`/`full_name`, e.g. `{"name":
   "purchase_orders", "full_name": "demo.sales.purchase_orders", ...}`),
   matching `back/core/databricks/uc/MetadataService.py`'s actual Unity
   Catalog fetch shape. **No production metadata tolerance for
   `catalog`/`schema`/`table` was added anywhere** — the fixture was wrong,
   not the production contract, per this closure's explicit instruction.
   Diff is minimal: only the 4 malformed table objects changed, compact
   JSON formatting preserved for every untouched line.
2. tests/eval/test_staged_dataset_metadata_shape.py (new, 9 tests)
   RED-first proof of #1: asserts neither mirrored dataset uses the stale
   shape, every metadata table carries `name`+`full_name` (`full_name`
   ending with `name`), the specific `staged-locked-anchor-dedup-001` row
   resolves to the exact expected table, and — the strongest regression
   guard — calls the REAL `agents.tools.metadata.tool_get_metadata`/
   `tool_get_table_detail` functions (via a real `ToolContext`) against
   every staged row's metadata and asserts no table entry ever has a null
   `name`/`full_name`, catching this exact bug at its source rather than
   only checking JSON field names. Plus a byte-identical-mirrors guard.
3. tests/eval/staged_contract.py (Important — explicit detection-failure
   diagnostics)
   `score_staged_examples_live()` now calls `_run_detection_for_example()`
   once, explicitly, per detect row — reusing the exact same cached call
   `_score_constraint()` already made (no extra live round-trip: still one
   LLM call per detect row) — and reports a new
   `detection_returned_valid_structured_output` dimension (1.0/0.0) plus a
   `[STAGED LIVE DETECTION FAILED]` diagnostic print naming the row and
   explicitly stating "not a dedup miss" whenever `detect_entities()`
   rejects/fails, so this failure mode is never again indistinguishable
   from a real anchor/alternate-label dedup miss. No threshold changed;
   the deterministic `owl_generator.staged_contract: 0.950` gate is
   untouched.
4. tests/eval/test_run_agent_owl_generator.py
   (`TestScoreStagedExamplesLiveReportsDetectionFailureExplicitly`, 3 new
   tests) RED-first proof of #3: a prose (non-JSON) fake reply scores
   `detection_returned_valid_structured_output=0.0` and prints a diagnostic
   naming the row + "not a dedup miss"/"dedup"; a valid-JSON reply scores
   `1.0`; the diagnostic costs zero extra live calls (still exactly one
   `call_serving_endpoint`/`detect_entities` call per detect row).
5. tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py (Important — tracing gap)
   New `_init_live_tracing(tracking_uri, experiment_name)`: sets
   `mlflow.set_tracking_uri()` then calls `agents.tracing.setup_tracing()`
   — never passed `host`/`token` (its only parameter is the experiment
   name, so no secret can be logged through this call by construction,
   mirroring `agents.tracing._safe_inputs`'s own exclusion set) — and
   prints an `[TRACING] ... -> enabled/DISABLED` diagnostic. Called from
   `main()` under `--live`, *before* constructing the `live_runner`
   lambda and before `run_contract(...)` — i.e. before `run_contract`'s own
   per-example loop makes its first live call to
   `_live_runner`/`staged.detect_entities`, and before
   `score_staged_examples_live`'s completion-chain calls. Offline
   (non-`--live`) mode never calls this — zero MLflow side effects, as
   before.
6. tests/eval/test_run_agent_owl_generator.py
   (`TestLiveModeInitializesTracingBeforeAnyFoundationModelCall`, 5 new
   tests) RED-first proof of #5: `_init_live_tracing` calls
   `setup_tracing(experiment_name=...)` with no `host`/`token` kwarg at
   all; its diagnostic print never contains a token value; `main()` calls
   tracing setup before `run_contract` and before `_live_runner` actually
   fire (proven via call-order tracking with monkeypatched collaborators,
   using a real secret-shaped token string in `sys.argv` to prove it never
   leaks into stdout); offline mode never initializes tracing.
7. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md §10
   Marked live-run attempt 1 (`218202e1...`) as a **FAILED live evaluation
   caused by the dataset fixture bug** (not a code defect) — recorded
   truthfully with the full root-cause explanation rather than deleted —
   and added the new passing attempt 2 (`68ee4e8e...`) with its full metric
   breakdown and trace-evidence confirmation (see Tests below).

