## Fix: live id-bracketing false rejection in Stage-3 completion (bare-id catalog + enum-constrained response_format)

### Context

Blocking bug reproduced live by the user: Stage-3 completion failed after
13.1s with `relations: references unknown or excluded entity id(s):
[Agent], [Call], [Claim], [Contract], [Customer], [Customerjourneyevent],
[Energyasset], [Financialdocument], [Interaction], [Invoice], [Meter],
[Meterreading], [Payment], [Person], [Subscription],
[cand-3a295986dc3f], [cand-6d2837cbaf28]`.

Root cause: `agents.agent_owl_generator.prompts._entity_catalog` rendered
each entity as `  • [{entity.id}] {label}` and the closure rule said
"reference entities ONLY by the ids listed above" — the model copied the
*bracketed* token (e.g. `[Agent]`) verbatim as the `domain`/`range` value.
`GenerateDraft.validate_references` compares against the **bare** id from
`closed_entity_ids()`, so every reference was rejected — a prompt-format-
induced id mismatch, not a real closure violation (the `cand-*` ids in the
error prove detection/inclusion worked correctly; only the id *format* was
wrong).

### Changes (two layers, no schema-repair/rewrite loop added — reject-only unweakened)

1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
   Prompt-only layer, insufficient alone (a prompt cannot structurally stop
   a non-compliant model — same lesson as the prior Stage-1 fix).
   `_entity_catalog` now renders each entity as a bare
   `- id: <value>\n  label: <value>` pair — never bracketed or quoted.
   `_CLOSURE_RULE` rewritten to explicitly forbid brackets/quotes/label
   substitution, with a worked counter-example (`id: Agent` → use `Agent`,
   never `[Agent]`, never `"Agent"`). Also reworded the trailing
   instruction in `build_relations_user_prompt`/`build_attributes_user_
   prompt`/`build_axioms_user_prompt` from "Return the `<X>` JSON." to "Now
   infer and provide the `<x>`." — a SEPARATE quirk surfaced only by this
   same revision's `response_format` change: live probing of
   `databricks-claude-sonnet-5` showed that once a completion substage
   sends `response_format` for the first time, the old trailing phrasing
   occasionally made the model double-encode its answer (a JSON *string*
   holding the real answer nested inside the top-level array key, e.g.
   `{"relations": "{\"relations\": [...]}"}"`), which fails
   `parse_relations_payload`. The new phrasing was verified live to answer
   correctly, repeatably. Wording-only — no lenient/tolerant parsing was
   added for the double-encoded shape.
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py`
   Structural layer, the actual fix. Added `_AXIOM_KINDS`, `_closed_id_enum`
   (a fresh `{"type": "string", "enum": sorted(ids)}` dict per call — never
   shared by reference across fields), and
   `build_relations_response_format`/`build_attributes_response_format`/
   `build_axioms_response_format`: strict `json_schema` payloads
   (`additionalProperties: false`, explicit `required`) whose id-valued
   fields (`domain`/`range`/`subject`/`object`) are each an `enum` of
   exactly `draft.closed_entity_ids()`. `axioms`' `kind` is constrained to
   the same 3-value enum the prompt documents
   (`subClassOf`/`disjointWith`/`equivalentClass`). Because the id fields
   are an enum, a bracketed or invented id is now structurally impossible
   on any endpoint that honours `response_format` — not merely instructed
   against.
3. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
   Added `_completion_response_format(builder, draft)`: builds the
   substage's enum-constrained schema from `draft.closed_entity_ids()`, or
   returns `None` when the closed set is empty (rather than building an
   impossible empty `enum`) so completion falls back to the strengthened
   bare-id prompt as the safety net. `_run_completion` now accepts and
   forwards `response_format` to `call_serving_endpoint`, always with
   `tools=None` (completion never reads documents/metadata, so there is no
   tools/response_format conflict to guard). `infer_relations`/
   `infer_attributes`/`infer_axioms` each now pass
   `_completion_response_format(schemas.build_*_response_format, draft)`.
   `validate_references` is unchanged and still runs unconditionally on
   every substage's parsed output — reject-only, never trust the wire even
   with schema enforcement; an unsupported `response_format` degrades
   transparently via the existing per-endpoint ban cache in
   `agents.engine_base.call_serving_endpoint` (same fallback mechanism as
   the prior Stage-1 fix).
4. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py`
   Added `TestRelationsResponseFormat`/`TestAttributesResponseFormat`/
   `TestAxiomsResponseFormat`: strict-schema shape, `additionalProperties`,
   required fields, enum contents built from an arbitrary id set, distinct
   dict objects per field (no accidental shared-reference enum), and the
   `kind` enum for axioms.
5. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
   Added: bare-id catalog rendering (`test_entity_catalog_renders_bare_ids_
   without_brackets`); closure-rule wording forbidding brackets/quotes,
   shared across relations/attributes/axioms prompts
   (`test_closure_rule_forbids_bracketed_or_quoted_ids`,
   `test_closure_rule_wording_shared_by_attributes_and_axioms_prompts`);
   per-substage `response_format` wiring with the enum built from
   `closed_entity_ids()` and `tools=None`; a bracketed-id answer still
   rejected reject-only with exactly one LLM call (no second finalization);
   an unsupported `response_format` degrading transparently end-to-end
   (`TestCompletionResponseFormatFallbackIntegration`); and the trailing
   double-encoding-trigger regression
   (`test_completion_user_prompts_avoid_the_return_json_double_encoding_
   trigger`).
6. `tests/eval/staged_contract.py`
   Added `_c_rejects_bracketed_id_ref`, mapped to the new
   `rejects_bracketed_id_reference` constraint kind — a real behavioural
   check (scripts a `[cand-...]`-shaped domain/range answer and asserts
   rejection with no rewrite), never the neutral-1.0 "unmapped kind"
   default. Added `TestRejectsBracketedIdReferenceCheck` unit tests for the
   new check function itself.
7. `tests/eval/test_staged_contract.py`
   Unit tests pinning `_c_rejects_bracketed_id_ref`'s behavior.
8. `tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py`
   `_MIN_STAGED_EXAMPLES` raised `15` -> `16`;
   `_REQUIRED_STAGED_CONSTRAINT_KINDS` extended with
   `rejects_bracketed_id_reference` so the new dimension can't silently
   disappear from the dataset.
9. `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl` and
   `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl` (byte-identical
   mirrors)
   Appended `staged-bracketed-id-rejection-001`: a `complete_relations` row
   built from the exact live-bug shape (one locked anchor + one included
   candidate, `cand-6`) whose scripted constraint requires rejection of a
   `[cand-6]`-bracketed reference with no post-rejection rewrite.
10. `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md`
    Documented the bare-id catalog + transport-level enum enforcement in
    §3a; added the `stage_completion_bare_id_enforcement` row (**scored**,
    unlike the Stage-1 transport row, via `rejects_bracketed_id_reference`)
    to §5's staged table; added the "Id-bracketing false rejection"
    failure-mode row to §6 with full root-cause/fix detail; raised the
    dataset floor `15` -> `16` and documented the new regression row in §7;
    appended the full sign-off entry to §10 with RED/GREEN evidence, both
    live results, and the double-encoding-wording secondary finding.

### RED/GREEN evidence

RED confirmed by running the new tests against the pre-fix source (no
