## Fix residual JSON double-encoding under response_format json_schema in Stage-3 completion parsing

### Context

Flagged as the residual bug by the prior "id-bracketing" completion fix
above: its "Secondary finding" only reworded a trailing prompt instruction
("Return the `<X>` JSON." → "Now infer and provide the `<x>`."), which
reduced but did not eliminate the underlying transport intermittency — the
same fix's own informational live-scoring section already showed
`infer_attributes` FAIL with `output must contain a 'attributes' list`
on a real `databricks-claude-sonnet-5` run.

Under `response_format` json_schema, Claude Sonnet endpoints
(`databricks-claude-sonnet-5`, and the user's own
`benoit_cayla.ontobricks-todrop.monclaudesonnetamoi`) intermittently
double-encode the structured answer in two possible shapes: (a) a
list-typed field's value comes back as a JSON-encoded STRING instead of
the raw array (e.g. `{"attributes": "[{...}]"}"`, tripping
`_require_list`'s `'attributes' must be a list` check), or (b) the ENTIRE
payload comes back as a JSON string holding the real object as its value
(`content = "{\"attributes\": [...]}"`, tripping `parse_json_object`'s
`structured output must be a JSON object` check).

### Changes (deterministic, reject-only preserved — NOT prose parsing)

1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py`
   Added `_unwrap_double_encoded(value, expected)`: undoes AT MOST ONE
   level of JSON-string double-encoding. Only when *value* is itself a
   `str` is a single extra `json.loads` attempted; the decoded result is
   used only if it is already an instance of *expected* — otherwise
   *value* is returned unchanged (no loop, no regex/prose extraction).
   Applied in two places: `parse_json_object`, when the top-level decode
   yields a `str` (whole-payload shape — accepted only if the one extra
   decode yields a `dict`); and `_require_list` plus
   `parse_detection_payload`'s `candidate_entities` getter, when the
   field's value is a `str` (field-level shape — accepted only if the one
   extra decode yields a `list`). A shape still wrong after the one
   tolerated decode (a plain sentence, a number, triple-encoding, a
   decoded list of non-dict items) is rejected with the same pre-existing
   clear message, with no further decoding. `validate_references` and the
   closure/ordering checks are entirely unchanged.
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
   No code change required: `_run_completion`'s attempt loop already only
   retries on `finish_reason == "length"` (output truncation), never on
   `SchemaValidationError` — a still-invalid-after-one-decode answer was
   already returned immediately as `rejected=True` with exactly one LLM
   call, and remains so.
3. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py`
   Added `TestWholePayloadDoubleEncodingTolerance` (5 tests: whole-payload
   double-encoded acceptance, still-rejects-triple-encoded,
   still-rejects-a-plain-json-encoded-sentence, still-rejects-a-
   json-encoded-number, normal-payload-unchanged) and
   `TestFieldLevelDoubleEncodingTolerance` (8 tests: field-level
   double-encoded acceptance for relations/attributes/axioms/detection
   `candidate_entities`, still-rejects-triple-encoded,
   still-rejects-a-non-json-string, still-rejects-a-json-string-decoding-
   to-a-number, still-validates-item-shape-after-unwrap).
4. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
   Added to `TestInferAttributes`: `test_double_encoded_attributes_field_
   is_accepted`, `test_whole_payload_double_encoded_is_accepted` (both
   end-to-end through the real orchestrator, `mock_llm.call_count == 1`),
   and `test_still_invalid_after_one_decode_is_rejected_no_second_call`
   (triple-encoded field, `rejected=True`, exactly one LLM call — no
   second finalization call).
5. `tests/eval/staged_contract.py`
   Added `_c_accepts_double_encoded_list_field`, mapped to the new
   `accepts_double_encoded_list_field` constraint kind — builds the
   completion draft from the dataset row's own `input.draft` (never a
   hand-picked literal), scripts a double-encoded `attributes` field
   answer, and asserts `infer_attributes` succeeds with the correctly
   unwrapped `domain` — a real behavioural check, never the neutral-1.0
   "unmapped kind" default.
6. `tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py`
   `_MIN_STAGED_EXAMPLES` raised `16` -> `17`.
7. `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl` and
   `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl`
   (byte-identical mirrors)
   Appended `staged-double-encoded-payload-001`: a `complete_attributes`
   row (one locked anchor + one included candidate, `cand-6`) whose
