### RED/GREEN evidence

RED confirmed by running the 13 new `test_owl_generator_schemas.py` tests
against the pre-fix source (no `_unwrap_double_encoded` in `schemas.py`):
exactly 5 failures — `test_whole_payload_double_encoded_json_string_is_
accepted`, and the 4 field-level `*_is_unwrapped` tests for
attributes/relations/axioms/detection — all with the pre-fix rejection
messages (`structured output must be a JSON object` /
`output must contain a '<key>' list`); the 8 still-reject/unchanged tests
in the same run already passed, as expected, since those code paths were
untouched by the fix. GREEN after implementing `_unwrap_double_encoded`
and wiring it into `parse_json_object`/`_require_list`/
`parse_detection_payload`: all 47 tests in the file pass, plus the 3 new
`test_owl_generator_staged.py::TestInferAttributes` integration tests.

