## Generate wizard: rename Class -> Entity, clarify Relationship/Attribute, add Start Over

### Context

User-approved frontend-only fix batch for the Generate ontology wizard
(`_ontology_wizard.html` + `ontology-wizard.js` / `ontology-wizard-review.js`):
(1) the wizard and Help Center glossary still showed the technical OWL term
"Class" to end users instead of the app's established "Entity" vocabulary;
(2) the Add/Edit candidate "Type hint" dropdown offered bare "Object
Property" / "Data Property" options with no link back to the app's existing
friendly split (Entities / Relationships / Attributes), which field
feedback flagged as ambiguous; (3) Stage 3 (Complete) had no way back to
Configure — only a hidden Retry button — unlike Stage 2, which already had
a "Discard Draft" button wired to `discardDraft()`. No backend/agents code
was touched; `value="class"` / `value="object_property"` /
`value="data_property"` and the `stats.classes_added` data key are
unchanged — only user-visible label text and wizard navigation changed.

