## Collapse inverse Generate relations to one direction

Context: Stage 3 `infer_relations` was emitting both directions of the same
fact (for example `handles` A→B and `handled` B→A). The prompt already
forbade bidirectional relations, but merge only deduped exact
`(domain, range, label)` tuples, so both object properties landed in the
ontology. Collapse inverses deterministically and keep the active-voice
direction.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py
   Relations system prompt: never emit a relation and its inverse; worked
   example is handles vs handled / owns vs ownedBy.
2. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py
   `drop_inverse_relations` keeps the higher active-voice score direction
   per unordered entity pair; `parse_relations_payload` applies it.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateWorkflow.py
   Merge skips a relation whose reverse directed pair is already present
   (defense in depth for older checkpoints).
4. tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py
   Parser keeps `handles` and drops `handled`; unrelated pairs stay.
5. tests/units/ontology/test_generate_workflow.py
   Merge of a handles/handled checkpoint adds one ObjectProperty.
6. tests/eval/staged_contract.py, tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py,
   tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl,
   .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl
   New `drops_inverse_relations` constraint and
   `staged-no-inverse-relations-001` row; staged example floor 17 → 18.
7. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md
   New §6 failure mode for inverse duplicate relations.
8. docs/user-guide.md
   Complete step notes that inverse pairs collapse to the active-voice
   direction.

