## Add the explicit Show in Explorer bridge

Context: Task 4 of the `staged-ontology-generate`/query-shell follow-up plan.
`SPARQLPlayground` already kept Run on the SPARQL tab and gated
`sparqlExploreBtn` on triple-shaped columns via a guarded `showInExplorer()`
stub. This task wires that explicit action to a new `SigmaGraph.loadQueryResults`
bridge so clicking "Show in Explorer" — and only that click — navigates to the
Explorer section and renders the current SPARQL rows. Run continues to never
navigate.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js`
   Add `SigmaGraph.loadQueryResults(results, columns)` to the module's public
   API: guards on non-empty array input, shows the graph-loading overlay,
   awaits `_waitForGraphLibs(10000)`, and on failure hides the overlay and
   emits a `showNotification(..., 'error')` without throwing. On success it
   defensively copies `results`/`columns` into `lastQueryResults`, calls the
   existing `buildGraph`, resets selection/hover/search state exactly like
   `_expandAndRenderGraph`, and calls `_render()`.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-execute.js`
   Replace the `showInExplorer()` guard stub with the real bridge: re-checks
   `currentResult` is non-empty and triple-shaped, calls
   `SidebarNav.switchTo('sigmagraph')`, then after a 150ms tick (letting the
   section become visible) calls `SigmaGraph.loadQueryResults(rows, columns)`
   and surfaces a fallback notification if it returns `false`. Run's
   `execute()` body is untouched — no sidebar switch was added there.
3. `tests/units/front/test_sparql_playground_contract.py`
   Add `test_explorer_bridge_is_explicit_and_sigma_accepts_query_rows`,
   asserting `SigmaGraph.loadQueryResults` is called from
   `query-execute.js`, `loadQueryResults:` is defined on `SigmaGraph`, and the
   explicit `SidebarNav.switchTo('sigmagraph')` call exists outside of
   `execute()` (already covered by the pre-existing
   `test_sparql_controller_has_samples_and_no_automatic_explorer_switch`).
4. `tests/e2e/dtwin/test_dtwin_flows.py`
   Add `TestQueryPlayground::test_show_in_explorer_stays_disabled_for_non_triples`,
   confirming `#sparqlExploreBtn` stays disabled on the default (non-triple)
   sample query — i.e. no implicit path ever enables/triggers the bridge.

