## Fix Task 4 review Important findings (self-sufficient loader, no timer, dedup notification)

Context: Code review of "Add the explicit Show in Explorer bridge" found
three Important findings and one adjacent Minor. The user chose the hardened
implementation over the original timer handoff: `SigmaGraph.loadQueryResults`
must not depend on `SigmaGraph.init()` having been scheduled elsewhere, the
150ms timer coupling in `showInExplorer()` must go, and a graph-library
failure must produce exactly one user notification. Also strengthened the
weak Task 4 tests (pure string presence / a statically-disabled button) into
real behavioral coverage.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js`
   `loadQueryResults` now calls `_loadGraphLibs()` itself (no longer relies
   on `SigmaGraph.init()`'s call). It also claims `_graphFilterActive` and
   caches `lastQueryResults` **synchronously, before its first `await`**, so
   a `SigmaGraph.init()` concurrently scheduled by query.js's
   `sidebarSectionChanged` → 100ms timer sees the flag already set and takes
   its "already active" branch instead of resetting `d3NodesData` /
   `d3LinksData` / `_graph` out from under the rows being loaded. On a
   library-load failure it restores the prior flag/cache (so a failed load
   can't mask an existing, already-rendered graph as "active") and no
   longer calls `showNotification` itself — it `console.error`s and returns
   `false`, leaving the single user-facing toast to the caller.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-execute.js`
   `showInExplorer()` drops the `window.setTimeout(..., 150)` handoff:
   after validating rows/columns it calls `SidebarNav.switchTo('sigmagraph')`
   then chains `SigmaGraph.loadQueryResults(rows, columns).then(...)`
   directly — no timer, and the sole failure notification lives here.
3. `tests/units/front/test_sparql_playground_contract.py`
   Strengthened `test_explorer_bridge_is_explicit_and_sigma_accepts_query_rows`
   with a `showInExplorer()` body-order assertion (no `setTimeout`, `switchTo`
   before `loadQueryResults`). Added
   `test_load_query_results_starts_its_own_lib_load_before_waiting` (proves
   `_loadGraphLibs()` precedes `await _waitForGraphLibs()`) and
   `test_load_query_results_claims_graph_filter_state_before_any_await`
   (proves `_graphFilterActive = true` is set before the function's first
   `await`).
4. `tests/e2e/dtwin/test_dtwin_flows.py`
   Replaced the "statically disabled button" check with
   `test_show_in_explorer_switches_then_loads_sigma_bridge_with_query_rows`:
   mocks `/dtwin/execute` (`page.route`) with a triple-shaped result, runs
   the query through the real UI to prove `#sparqlExploreBtn` goes from
   disabled to enabled, stubs `SidebarNav.switchTo` / `SigmaGraph.
   loadQueryResults` to record call order/args, clicks Show in Explorer, and
   asserts `switchTo` fires before `loadQueryResults` with the exact
   executed rows/columns — deterministic and network-independent.

